# The `.gitkeep` keeps this directory in the repository even though it
# conceptually represents a *destination* tree the tests prepare by
# writing files into a tmp copy. Tests using it do:
#
#     import shutil, tmp_path
#     shutil.copytree(_FIX / "collision-in-destination", tmp_path / "dest")
#
# and then call `DryRunService.plan(..., destination=tmp_path / "dest")`.
# The `.gitkeep` is the only committed content; the "collisions" the
# tests detect are seeded by the test itself (e.g. a `pyproject.toml`
# with content "old") so the fixture remains useful for other scenarios
# without carrying a file that would need to be committed *and*
# hash-checked.
